  "rating": {
    "inherent": "high",
    "residual": "high",
    "forecast": "high",
    "rationale": "Present design risk is dominated by two issues: irreversible refund issuance from trusted staff requests with only behavioral prompt checking, and missing attributable provenance because refunds use a shared service account while no durable request record links actions to a staff member. The prompt-based check lowers the refund path one tier to moderate, but the separate repudiation property finding remains high because declared logging does not restore attribution. Forecast stays high because the current design already lacks structural controls whose removal or decay would materially worsen the top finding."
  },
  "limitations": [
